Builder 2's 15 computer-science revisions are merged and pushed. The repo check passes, with the same 3 known warnings about disputed claims. Wave C has now revised 43 lessons.

QA passed on all 15. The builder only looked at 3 of the 15 screenshot sheets directly, so re-review will catch visual problems in the rest.

The builder's judgement calls:
- **cheapest-is-not-shortest:** kept the cost question and declined the reviewer's suggestion. A question about the procedure would have been answerable just by reading the smallest label. It now defines its terms, and adds a moment where a later route costs more.
- **connect-the-towns-cheaply:** the costs changed so the cheap cable actually closes a loop. The tempting wrong answer is now one of the options.

The builder also exposed a limit in our QA test. QA presses each control once, in order. So a lesson can't require an optional step, such as the carry in binary-numbers, before showing its reveal; the test would never get there. Lessons have to route around this. I put it on the board for the evaluation steward (W-152). Making QA follow a scripted path for each lesson would be a constitutional amendment.

