- Bram's review of the knot library's evaluator;
- review batch 10;
- Kiri's fix for the kit's contrast colours.

You are a demo builder in System 3 Company. This is board W-155. After the visual designer's kit token fix (K1 and K6, now merged: text-safe --good/--warn/--bad in the light theme, plus new --good-fill/--warn-fill/--bad-fill for fills), 18 published lessons still fail colour contrast because of colours in their own code. Read CLAUDE.md, company/roles/demo-builder.md, company/design/system.md (the token table) and company/reviews/_accessibility/2026-10-13-published-audit.md, both batches. Each lesson's findings are in company/reviews/<slug>/2026-10-1[34]-accessibility.md. Work in your worktree and commit there (don't push). Never use pkill: use tools/serve.sh.

1. Find the 18 lessons: the 26 failures listed in the audit, minus the 8 now passing (clicks-not-value, lopsided-tree, overfitting, small-hospital-big-swings, supply-demand, water-follows-the-crowd, jackpot-once-a-week, say-seventy-mean-it).
2. In each one, fix the failing text colours:
   - use text-safe tokens (`--good`, `--warn`, `--bad`, `--fg`, `--muted`) for text;
   - use the *-fill tokens only for fills and shapes;
   - replace hard-coded pastels used as text;
   - fix white text on mid-green fills, e.g. use dark text or a darker fill;
   - never use `--domain` as body text on a light card;
   - keep the meaning, and never rely on colour alone.
   Change no pedagogy and no claims. A colour-only fix needs no version bump, but say so in a build.md note.
3. Re-run `node tools/a11y-scan.mjs` on the 18 against a build of your worktree (`NEXT_DIST_DIR=.next-c18 npx next build`, then `git checkout tsconfig.json`, then `tools/serve.sh start 3441 .next-c18`; stop the server afterwards). Then run lesson QA on all 18 (`QA_ONLY`; the feed-chips failures are known, W-136) and `npm run check`.
Report in under 150 words: the commit hash, and pass/fail per lesson after the fix.

